        "faqs": [
          {
            "q": " What is the best time for a Ladakh bike trip?",
            "a": "The best time for a Ladakh bike trip is June to September when the highways from Manali to Leh and Srinagar to Leh are open. The weather is clear, the roads are (mostly) snow-free, and you’ll get breathtaking views of Ladakh’s rugged landscapes.\n\nStart planning your [Leh Ladakh Bike Trip](https://indiatour.live/tours/umling-la-hanle-ladakh-bike-trip) here!"
          },
          {
            "q": "What is the best route for Leh - Nubra - Pangong - Leh?",
            "a": "The most popular route for this circuit is:\n\n**Day 1:** Leh → [Khardung La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/khardung-la) → Nubra Valley (Diskit/Hunder)\n\n**Day 2:** Nubra Valley → Shyok Route → [Pangong Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pangong-tso)\n\n**Day 3:** Pangong Lake → Chang La → Leh\n\n**Alternative Route:** Nubra → Wari La → Pangong (Less crowded but challenging)"
          },
          {
            "q": "How much distance will I cover on this Leh - Nubra - Pangong - Leh circuit?",
            "a": "**Leh to Nubra Valley:** ~160 km (5-6 hrs)\n\n**Nubra Valley to Pangong:** ~200 km (6-7 hrs)\n\n**Pangong to Leh:** ~230 km (6-7 hrs)\n\n**Total: ~600 km in 3 days!**"
          },
          {
            "q": "Can I complete Nubra to Pangong in one day?",
            "a": "Yes, but it’s a long and challenging ride (6-7 hrs). The Shyok route is the fastest but has tricky sections. If unsure, break the journey with a stop at Durbuk or Tangste.\n\n"
          },
          {
            "q": "Do I need prior biking experience for this trip?",
            "a": "Short answer: YES! This isn’t a casual Sunday ride. Ladakh’s roads throw high-altitude passes, river crossings, and sharp hairpin bends your way. If you’ve never done long-distance or off-road biking, consider a shorter Himalayan ride first."
          },
          {
            "q": "What is included in this bike trip package?",
            "a": "This package is designed to give you a complete, hassle-free Ladakh riding experience. It includes your bike with fuel, riding gear, comfortable stays, meals, all necessary permits, Volvo transfers, an experienced trip leader, on-ground mechanic support, and a backup vehicle for assistance throughout the journey."
          },
          {
            "q": "Do I need a permit for Leh Ladakh?",
            "a": "Yes, Inner Line Permits are required for visiting Nubra Valley, Pangong Lake, Hanle, and Umling La. Don’t worry we’ve got it covered. All necessary permits are included in your package and will be arranged by our team, so you can focus purely on the ride."
          },
          {
            "q": "Can I ride this circuit in winter?",
            "a": "Not recommended! Heavy snowfall blocks [Khardung La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/khardung-la), Chang La & Shyok route in winter (Nov–April). Best to ride June–Sept for safe travel."
          }
        ]
