        "faqs": [
          {
            "q": "How many days are required for a Srinagar to Ladakh bike trip?",
            "a": "A 10–11 day itinerary is ideal to cover Srinagar, Leh, Nubra, [Pangong](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pangong-tso), Hanle, [Umling La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/umling-la), and return via Manali comfortably."
          },
          {
            "q": " Is Srinagar to Leh route better than Manali to Leh?",
            "a": "Yes, the Srinagar route allows gradual altitude gain, making acclimatization easier and offering more scenic landscapes."
          },
          {
            "q": "What is the best time for this bike trip?",
            "a": "The best time is from June to September when both Srinagar-Leh and Leh-Manali highways are open and accessible.\nCheck [Umling La Ladakh Bike Trip](https://indiatour.live/tours/umling-la-hanle-ladakh-bike-trip) here!\n "
          },
          {
            "q": "Are riding gears included in the package?",
            "a": "Yes, your safety is fully taken care of. The package includes essential riding gear such as helmets for both rider and pillion, riding jackets, and knee guards so you can focus on enjoying the journey without worrying about gear arrangements."
          },
          {
            "q": "Do I need permits for this trip?",
            "a": "Yes, Inner Line Permits are required for visiting Nubra Valley, Pangong Lake, Hanle, and Umling La. Don’t worry we’ve got it covered. All necessary permits are included in your package and will be arranged by our team, so you can focus purely on the ride."
          },
          {
            "q": "How difficult is this Ladakh bike trip?",
            "a": "This trip is moderately to highly challenging due to long riding hours, high altitudes, and mixed terrain, especially near Umling La."
          },
          {
            "q": "Which bike is best for this trip?",
            "a": "Royal Enfield Himalayan, or similar high-powered bikes are ideal for long-distance and high-altitude riding."
          },
          {
            "q": "Are fuel stations available on this route?",
            "a": "Fuel stations are available in Manali and Leh, but are limited or unavailable in remote regions along the route. However, there’s no need to worry this trip includes fuel for the entire journey, with arrangements made in advance by India Tour Experiences. "
          }
        ]
