            "description": "- Today we ride from Pangong Lake towards Hanle, one of Ladakh’s most remote regions.\n- On the way, we will pass the town of Chushul and then stop at the Rezang La War Memorial, paying tribute to the heroes who laid down their lives for their motherland in the 1962 Indo–China War.\n- The ride opens up to vast Changthang landscapes with views of the Black Mountain and endless valleys.\n- On the way, stop for lunch and continue riding through the rugged landscape until we reach the charming village of Hanle.\n- Hanle is renowned as the site of the Indian Astronomical Observatory and India's first Dark Sky Reserve.\n- Thanks to clear skies and minimal light pollution, Hanle is ideal for stargazing and astrophotography.\n- At night, if the skies are clear, we step out to watch the Milky Way light up the sky.\n- Overnight stay in Hanle.\n- Breakfast and dinner included.\n- Riding Distance: 160 km",
