        "location": "Ladakh",
        "routeSummary": "with Tso Moriri & Tso Kar",
        "overviewText": "This 10-day Leh Ladakh adventure is packed with high-altitude thrills and offbeat gems. Ride through iconic mountain passes like [Khardung La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/khardung-la) and [Tanglang La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tanglang-la), witness the surreal beauty of [Pangong Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pangong-tso), Tso Moriri, and Tso Kar, and explore the cultural richness of [Diskit Monastery](https://indiatour.live/attractions/diskit-monastery) and Sham Valley.\n\nGet your adrenaline fix with a camel safari in the Hunder sand dunes, feel the magnetic pull at [Magnetic Hill](https://indiatour.live/attractions/magnetic-hill), and marvel at the natural confluence at Sangam Point. Travel along the dramatic Shyok River route, stay in handpicked locations, and soak in the raw, rugged beauty that defines Ladakh.\n\nPerfect for nature lovers, thrill-seekers, and photography buffs—this is Ladakh, the India Tour way.\n\n### **Route**\n\nLeh - Nubra - Khardungla - Shyok - Pangong - Tso Moriri - Tsokar & TanglangLa - Leh \n\n### **Why You Should Opt for This Thrilling Leh Ladakh**\n\n1. **Covers Ladakh’s Best-Kept Secrets**: From the iconic Pangong Lake to the lesser-known beauty of [Tso Moriri](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tso-moriri-lake) and Tso Kar, this trip is a complete visual feast.\n2. **Ultimate High-Altitude Experience**: Cross world-famous passes like [Khardung La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/khardung-la) and [Tanglang La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tanglang-la), with altitude, adventure, and awe in every mile.\n3. **Offbeat Meets Iconic**: Witness blockbuster spots like [Magnetic Hill](https://indiatour.live/attractions/magnetic-hill) and Sangam Point, while also taking the scenic Shyok route to uncover raw Ladakhi landscapes.\n4. **Cultural & Natural Mix**: Explore ancient monasteries like Diskit, ride camels in the cold desert of Hunder, and stay by lakes so blue they seem unreal.\n5. **Unmatched Value**: At just ₹24,950 (with ₹3,050 off in our Summer Sale), it’s one of the most value-packed Ladakh trips available—without cutting corners on comfort or experience.\n6. **Curated by Experts**: Backed by India Tour Experiences, this isn’t your regular tour. It’s thoughtfully planned, expertly guided, and perfectly paced.\n\n### **Essential Tips for Your Thrilling Leh Ladakh**\n\n- **✅ Acclimatize Properly**: Leh sits at over 11,000 ft—rest on Day 1, avoid exertion, and hydrate well to beat altitude sickness.\n- **✅ Pack for All Weather**: Days can be sunny, but nights turn freezing. Carry thermals, windproof jackets, gloves, and sunglasses—even in summer.\n- **✅ Carry Essentials**: Power banks, a refillable water bottle, basic medicines, sunscreen (SPF 50+), lip balm, and wet wipes are must-haves.\n- **✅ Cash is King**: ATMs are limited outside Leh. Carry enough cash for Nubra, [Pangong](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pangong-tso), and Tso Moriri—especially for food, entry fees, or local shopping.\n- **✅ Keep Permits Handy**: Inner Line Permits are mandatory for Nubra, Pangong, and [Tso Moriri](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tso-moriri-lake). Our team will arrange them—but keep a few photocopies with you.\n- **✅ Stay Charged (Mentally & Electrically)**: Mobile network is patchy; BSNL and Jio work best. Electricity may be limited in remote areas, so charge your devices whenever you can.\n- **✅ Respect the Terrain & Culture**: Don’t litter, avoid loud music at monasteries or lakes, and always ask before photographing locals.",
