      "overviewText": "This **9-day Delhi to Delhi Umling La Ladakh bike trip** is all about long-distance riding, extreme altitudes, and experiencing the complete Ladakh circuit from the plains to the Himalayas. Starting from Delhi, the journey takes you through Manali and into the high-altitude desert of Ladakh via some of the most iconic roads in India.\n\nThe ride from Manali to Leh via [Atal Tunnel](https://indiatour.live/attractions/atal-tunnel), Jispa, and Sarchu sets the tone for the adventure—dramatic landscapes, high mountain passes, and endless open roads. As you reach Leh, the journey continues towards [Nubra Valley](https://indiatour.live/attractions/nubra-valley) via Khardung La (17,982 ft), followed by the stunning ride to Pangong Lake, where crystal-clear waters meet rugged mountains.\n\nThe adventure intensifies as you head towards Hanle, one of the most remote regions in Ladakh, known for its clear skies and untouched beauty. From here, you ride to **[Umling La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/umling-la) (19,024 ft)**—one of the highest motorable roads in the world where every turn challenges your limits and rewards you with unmatched views.\n\nThe return journey via Sarchu and Manali completes a full circuit, bringing you back to Delhi after covering some of the most extreme terrains and scenic routes in the Himalayas.\n\nLong, challenging, and unforgettable this trip is for riders who want the ultimate Ladakh biking experience from start to finish.\n\n### **Delhi to Delhi Umling La Ladakh Bike Trip Route:**\n\nDelhi - Manali - [Sarchu](https://indiatour.live/attractions/sarchu) - Leh - Khardungla - Nubra - Pangong - Hanle - Umling La - Leh - Sarchu - Manali - Delhi\n\n### **Why You Should Opt for This Delhi to Delhi Umling La Ladakh Bike Trip**\n\nIf you’re looking for a complete [Delhi to Ladakh bike trip](https://indiatour.live/tours/leh-ladakh-bike-trip) that covers everything from highways to high-altitude extremes, this is it! Over 9 days, you’ll experience changing landscapes, remote regions, and some of the most iconic biking routes in India.\n\n**1. Complete Delhi to Ladakh Circuit:** Start from Delhi and ride all the way to Ladakh via Manali, covering the full Himalayan route instead of just local circuits.\n\n**2. Conquer Umling La – The Ultimate High-Altitude Ride:** Ride to Umling La (19,024 ft), one of the highest motorable roads in the world, offering a true test of endurance and skill.\n\n**3. Ride Through India’s Most Iconic Routes:** From Atal Tunnel and Sarchu to [Khardung La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/khardung-la) and Chang La, this trip covers legendary biking routes every rider dreams of.\n\n**4. Explore Ladakh’s Top Highlights:** Experience Nubra Valley, Pangong Lake, and [Hanle](https://indiatour.live/attractions/hanle) each offering completely different landscapes and experiences.\n\n**5. Long-Distance Riding Experience:** This trip isn’t just about destinations it’s about the journey. Cover long stretches, diverse terrains, and experience the transition from plains to high mountains.\n\n**6. A Perfect Mix of Adventure & Scenic Beauty:** From rugged terrains and high passes to serene lakes and open valleys, this trip offers a complete Ladakh experience.\n\nThis [Leh Ladakh bike trip](https://indiatour.live/tours/leh-to-leh-bike-trip-with-turtuk) isn’t just about riding it’s about completing one of the most iconic journeys in India. If you’re looking for a full-fledged adventure from [Delhi to Ladakh](https://indiatour.live/tours/umling-la-hanle-ladakh-bike-trip), this is the ultimate ride.\n\nExplore the Himalayas with our [Leh Ladakh bike trip](https://indiatour.live/tours/umling-la-tso-moriri-ladakh-bike-trip)!",
