      "faqs": [
        {
          "q": "What’s the Best Time for a Delhi to Umling La Bike Trip?",
          "a": "The ideal time to plan this journey is between June and September. During these months, the roads are open, the weather is relatively stable, and the scenery is at its best. Avoid traveling from October to May, as extreme winter conditions lead to heavy snowfall and closed mountain passes, making the route dangerous or inaccessible."
        },
        {
          "q": "Do I Need Prior Biking Experience?",
          "a": "Yes, this route is not for beginners. Umling La sits at a staggering 19,024 feet, making it the highest motorable road in the world. The terrain is rugged, with river crossings, steep inclines, and long stretches of isolation. Prior off-roading experience is crucial for your safety and confidence on such challenging paths."
        },
        {
          "q": "Are riding gears included in the package?",
          "a": "Yes, your safety is fully taken care of. The package includes essential riding gear such as helmets for both rider and pillion, riding jackets, and knee guards so you can focus on enjoying the journey without worrying about gear arrangements.\n\nRide through Khardung La – [Book Ladakh bike trip](https://indiatour.live/tours/ladakh-bike-trip-from-srinagar)!"
        },
        {
          "q": "What If My Bike Breaks Down?",
          "a": "No need to stress your trip is fully supported. We have a dedicated motorbike mechanic traveling with the group throughout the journey. In case of any breakdown, immediate on-road assistance will be provided. \n\nBook your guided [Ladakh motorcycle expedition](https://indiatour.live/tours/umling-la-hanle-ladakh-bike-trip-from-delhi) now!"
        },
        {
          "q": "What’s the Total Distance from Delhi to Umling La?",
          "a": "If you're riding from Delhi via Manali, it’s around 1,100 km to Leh. From Leh to Umling La via Hanle adds another 300 km. For a full round trip, expect to cover around 3,000 km."
        },
        {
          "q": "What Are the Best Bikes for the Trip?",
          "a": "For a journey like this, you’ll need a motorcycle built for endurance and rough terrain. Royal Enfield Himalayan is a top pick for its stability and off-road capabilities. Other solid options include the Royal Enfield Classic 500, Bajaj Dominar 400, and KTM Adventure 390. Whichever bike you choose, make sure it’s well-serviced and you carry basic spare parts."
        },
        {
          "q": "Do I Need Permits for Umling La and Hanle?",
          "a": "Yes, Inner Line Permits are required for visiting Nubra Valley, [Pangong Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pangong-tso), Hanle, and Umling La. Don’t worry we’ve got it covered. All necessary permits are included in your package and will be arranged by our team, so you can focus purely on the ride."
        },
        {
          "q": "How Can I Avoid Altitude Sickness?",
          "a": "To avoid Acute Mountain Sickness (AMS), spend at least two full days acclimatizing in Leh before heading higher. Drink plenty of water—at least 3 to 4 liters a day—avoid alcohol and smoking, and consult your doctor if you plan to take Diamox. Ascend gradually and don’t rush the journey."
        }
      ]
