      "flightIncluded": false,
      "flights_included": false,
      "location": "Ladakh",
      "routeSummary": "Delhi - Manali - Leh - Srinagar",
      "overviewText": "If Ladakh’s been calling you, this is your sign to go. This 11-day, 10-night journey from Delhi to Srinagar isn’t just a trip—it’s a full-blown adventure through the heart of the Himalayas.\n\nWe start from Delhi, head to Manali, and slowly climb our way up to Leh, letting you soak in every bit of the changing landscape. Think winding mountain roads, chilly streams, and little dhabas that serve the best Maggi with a view. From there, it’s a ride through all the iconic stops—Nubra’s desert dunes, the surreal blue of [Pangong Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pangong-tso), and finally, the fairytale ending in Srinagar.\n\nThe best part? You’re not doing this alone. You’re doing it with a bunch of like-minded travellers who, like you, want to explore, laugh, and make memories in the mountains. Whether you're coming solo or with friends, the trip is all planned out—stay, food, permits, logistics—so you don’t have to worry about a thing.\n\nJust pack your warmest jacket, charge your camera, and let the Himalayas do the rest.\n\n### Route\nDelhi - Manali - Jispa - [Sarchu](https://indiatour.live/attractions/sarchu) - Leh - Khardungla - Nubra - Turtuk - Nubra -Pangong - Chang La - Leh - [Kargil](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kargil) - [Sonmarg](https://indiatour.live/attractions/sonmarg) - Srinagar\n\n### **Why You Should Opt for This Ladakh Group Trip from Delhi**\n\n1. **Delhi to Srinagar—One Epic Ride Through the Himalayas:** This isn’t your average road trip. We start in Delhi, cruise through Manali’s pine forests, cross jaw-dropping passes like Baralacha La and Tanglang La, camp by the stars near [Pangong](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pangong-tso), explore ancient monasteries, and end the ride in the calm, lake-laced beauty of Srinagar. It’s the kind of journey that leaves you speechless and storytelling for years.\n\n2. **The Views? Unreal. The Vibes? Even Better:** From the otherworldly landscapes of Leh to the desert dunes of [Nubra](https://indiatour.live/attractions/nubra-valley) and the turquoise magic of Pangong Lake, every day on this trip feels like a postcard come to life. You’ll spot yaks, cross icy rivers, ride alongside massive mountains—and maybe even share a cup of tea with a monk.\n\n3. **Manali to Leh Highway—India’s Wildest Road:** This stretch is not for the faint of heart. Think steep climbs, sudden waterfalls, and valleys that’ll make you pause just to take it all in. It’s raw, it’s rugged, and it’s ridiculously rewarding. If you’ve ever wanted to feel tiny in the best way possible, this is it.\n\n4. **Travel With a Tribe:** You might come solo, but you won’t stay that way for long. This group trip is all about good company—fellow travellers who love mountains, road trips, and late-night card games just as much as you do. By the end, you’ll have a bunch of new friends and a shared photo album full of inside jokes.\n\n5. **Leave the Planning to Us:** Permits? Sorted. Stay? Booked. Food? Handled. All you need to do is show up with a solid jacket, your camera, and a big appetite for adventure. Whether it's your first Ladakh trip or your fifth, we take care of the boring bits so you can focus on the breathtaking ones.\n\n6. **A Journey Worth Every Mile:** You’ll wake up to snow peaks, ride through valleys, sip butter tea at roadside stalls, and watch the stars take over the sky in places your network can’t reach (and that’s a good thing). This is more than a trip—it’s a reset button for the soul.\n\n### **Essential Tips for Your Ladakh Group Trip from Delhi**\n\n- **✅ Acclimatize Like a Pro:** Ladakh isn’t your regular hill station. Altitude hits differently here. So, take those first couple of days slow—hydrate, rest, and let your body adjust before you start chasing mountain highs.\n\n- **✅ Pack Smart, Not Heavy:** Layers are your best friend. Days can be warm-ish, but mornings and nights? Cold enough to see your breath. Bring thermals, windproof jackets, gloves, and waterproof shoes. And yes—don’t skip sunscreen and lip balm. The sun *and* wind here are savage.\n\n- **✅ Carry a Basic Medical Kit:** We’ve got first aid on the trip, but it’s good to carry your own mini kit—think Diamox (for AMS), painkillers, bandaids, and any personal meds. And maybe some ginger candies—they’re great for altitude nausea.\n\n- **✅ Say Bye to Network:** You’ll be offline in a bunch of places (like Pangong and Nubra). Download your music, maps, and Insta drafts before the trip starts. Use this as a detox—you’ll come back with more stories than screen time.\n\n- **✅ Carry a Power Bank and Camera:** Charging spots can be limited in remote places, so a power bank is gold. And trust us—you’ll want a good camera or at least your phone fully juiced. The views are straight-up wallpaper material.\n\n- **✅ Restroom Realities in Ladakh:** You’ll get clean washrooms in hotels and camps, but during long drives, expect basic pitstops. Carry toilet paper, wet wipes, and hand sanitizer like a pro.\n\n- **✅ Cash Is King:** ATMs are few and not always functional. Withdraw cash in Leh or Manali and keep small denominations handy for local shopping, snacks, or that emergency Maggi stop.\n\n- **✅Don’t Overpack:** You won’t need ten outfits. Prioritize comfort and weather-appropriateness over style. You’ll end up wearing the same jacket in 80% of your photos anyway—and that’s okay.\n\n- **✅ Respect the Mountains:** Don’t litter, don’t honk unnecessarily, and always greet the locals with a smile. Ladakh gives you a lot—give back by being a mindful traveler.",
