      "faqs": [
        {
          "q": "What places will we cover on this trip?",
          "a": "Get ready to tick off Delhi, Manali, [Jispa](https://indiatour.live/attractions/jispa), Leh, Nubra Valley, Pangong Lake, [Kargil](https://indiatour.live/attractions/kargil), and Srinagar. Think of it as a greatest-hits album of the Himalayas—scenic roads, high-altitude passes, sparkling lakes, and charming towns."
        },
        {
          "q": "When’s the best time to go?",
          "a": "The trip runs between June and September—when the roads are open, skies are clear, and Ladakh’s landscapes are in full glory. You’ll get sunny days, starlit nights, and just the right amount of chill."
        },
        {
          "q": " I’ve never done a high-altitude trip before. Is this doable?",
          "a": "Absolutely! As long as you're reasonably fit and mentally ready for a bit of altitude and adventure, you're good. We give you enough time to acclimatize in Leh and take it slow where it counts."
        },
        {
          "q": "What’s the ride like? Is it tough?",
          "a": "Expect a mix of smooth highways, bumpy patches, and epic mountain passes. Some days you’ll cruise, others might feel like an off-roading challenge—but it’s all part of the thrill. Our backup crew’s got your back the whole way."
        },
        {
          "q": " Is this trip good for solo travellers?",
          "a": "100%. A lot of people join solo and end up finding their travel tribe here. Whether you’re shy or super social, the group vibes are welcoming, fun, and full of banter."
        },
        {
          "q": "How cold does it get? What should I pack?",
          "a": "It gets super chilly, especially early mornings and at high passes. Pack thermals, windproof jackets, gloves, and high-ankle shoes. Don’t forget sunscreen, lip balm, sunglasses, and a sense of humor."
        },
        {
          "q": "Will my phone work everywhere?",
          "a": "Short answer—no. You'll have good network in Manali, Leh, and Srinagar, but expect zero bars at places like Nubra, Pangong, and on the road. Honestly, it’s a blessing in disguise."
        },
        {
          "q": "What kind of food will be available?",
          "a": "You’ll get a mix of local Ladakhi food, comforting Indian meals, and some quick bites on the go. We make sure you’re well-fed, warm, and fueled for the ride ahead."
        }
      ]
