      "faqs": [
        {
          "q": "Is this trip suitable for first-time Ladakh travelers?",
          "a": "Yes! This itinerary is thoughtfully planned with gradual altitude gain and rest periods, making it ideal for both first-timers and seasoned travelers."
        },
        {
          "q": " What’s included in the package cost?",
          "a": "Inclusions typically cover:\n\n- Accommodation (6 nights)\n- Transportation in tempo traveler or SUV\n- Meals (breakfast & dinner)\n- Inner Line Permits\n- Experienced trip leader/driver\n- Sightseeing as per itinerary\n    \n    (Please check the detailed inclusions section at the time of booking.)"
        },
        {
          "q": "What’s the group size for this trip?",
          "a": "We keep our groups small and intimate—usually between 10 to 15 travelers—to ensure comfort, better coordination, and meaningful experiences."
        },
        {
          "q": "Do I need to carry cash or will cards work?",
          "a": "Cards and UPI work in Leh town, but cash is recommended for [Nubra](https://indiatour.live/attractions/nubra-valley), Pangong, [Tso Moriri](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tso-moriri-lake), and other remote locations. Carry small denominations for local purchases."
        },
        {
          "q": "What kind of clothing should I pack?",
          "a": "Layering is key. Carry:\n- Thermal innerwear\n- Fleece/woolen sweaters\n- Waterproof windcheater\n- Gloves, beanies, warm socks\n- UV sunglasses and sunscreen\n    \n    Even in summer, nights are cold in Ladakh."
        },
        {
          "q": "Is there mobile network connectivity throughout the trip?",
          "a": "Mobile signals are available only in Leh and sometimes in Nubra. Jio and BSNL work best. Expect no network at [Pangong](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pangong-tso), [Tso Moriri](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tso-moriri-lake), and high passes."
        },
        {
          "q": "Will I face altitude sickness?",
          "a": "Some mild symptoms (headache, breathlessness) are normal. Rest well on Day 1, stay hydrated, avoid smoking/alcohol, and consult your doctor for preventive meds if needed."
        },
        {
          "q": "Is this a road trip? What are the travel conditions like?",
          "a": "Yes, this is a scenic road trip across mountain terrain. Roads vary—from smooth highways to bumpy off-roads. But every stretch offers jaw-dropping views!"
        }
      ]
