      "overviewText": "This **11-day Delhi to Delhi Umling La & Tso Moriri Ladakh bike trip** is all about long-distance riding, extreme altitudes, and exploring Ladakh’s most remote and untouched regions. Starting from Delhi, the journey takes you through Manali and into the high-altitude desert via the iconic Leh-Manali highway.\n\nThe ride from Manali to Leh via Atal Tunnel, [Jispa](https://indiatour.live/attractions/jispa), and [Sarchu](https://indiatour.live/attractions/sarchu) sets the tone—dramatic landscapes, high mountain passes, and endless open roads. After exploring Leh, the journey continues towards Nubra Valley via [Khardung La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/khardung-la) (17,982 ft), followed by the scenic ride to Pangong Lake, where crystal-clear waters meet rugged mountains.\n\nThe adventure deepens as you head towards Hanle, one of Ladakh’s most remote regions known for its clear skies and raw beauty. From here, you ride to **[Umling La \\(19,024 ft\\)](https://indiatour.live/attractions/umling-la)**—one of the highest motorable roads in the world—before continuing to **[Tso Moriri](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tso-moriri-lake)**, a high-altitude lake known for its untouched landscapes and peaceful surroundings.\n\nThe return journey via Sarchu and Manali completes a full Himalayan circuit, bringing you back to Delhi after covering some of the most extreme and scenic routes in Ladakh.\n\nLong, immersive, and unforgettable—this trip is for riders who want to experience Ladakh at its highest, remotest, and most diverse.\n\nPlan your [Leh Ladakh Trip](https://indiatour.live/tours/umling-la-hanle-ladakh-bike-trip-from-delhi) with India Tour Experiences!\n\n### **Route:**\n\nDelhi - Manali - Sarchu - Leh - Khardungla - Nubra - Pangong - Hanle - Umling La - Tso Moriri - Sarchu - Manali - Delhi\n\n\n### **Why You Should Opt for This Delhi to Delhi Umling La & Tso Moriri Ladakh Bike**\n\nIf you’re looking for a Ladakh bike trip that goes beyond the usual routes and covers both extreme altitudes and remote landscapes, this is it! Over 11 days, you’ll experience a complete Himalayan circuit packed with adventure and variety.\n\n**1. Conquer Umling La – One of the Highest Roads in the World:** Ride to Umling La (19,024 ft), a true high-altitude challenge and one of the most rewarding experiences in Ladakh.\n\n**2. Explore Tso Moriri – Ladakh’s Hidden Gem:** Unlike Pangong, Tso Moriri offers a quieter, more untouched experience surrounded by vast landscapes and fewer crowds.\n\n**3. Ride Through Ladakh’s Most Iconic Routes:** From Atal Tunnel and Sarchu to [Khardung La](https://indiatour.live/attractions/khardung-la) and Chang La, this trip covers legendary biking routes across the Himalayas.\n\n**4. Experience Diverse Landscapes Every Day:** From lush valleys of Manali to cold deserts of Nubra and high-altitude lakes like Pangong and Tso Moriri, the scenery keeps changing throughout the journey.\n\n**5. Discover Remote Regions Like [Hanle](https://indiatour.live/attractions/hanle):** One of the most unique stops, Hanle offers clear night skies, isolation, and a rare glimpse into Ladakh’s untouched side.\n\n**6. Complete a Full Delhi to Delhi Circuit:** This trip offers a complete journey from plains to mountains and back, making it a full-fledged Himalayan adventure.\n\nThis [Leh Ladakh bike trip](https://indiatour.live/tours/leh-to-leh-bike-trip-with-turtuk) isn’t just about riding—it’s about experiencing [Ladakh](https://indiatour.live/tours/umling-la-hanle-ladakh-bike-trip) in its most extreme, raw, and beautiful form. If you’re looking for a longer, deeper, and more immersive adventure, this is the ultimate ride.",
